# Cloudflare Pages reads this ONLY at the root of public/. Do not move it.
#
# Extensionless → directory redirects, so /orbit and /spacetrack/signal reach
# the same page as their trailing-slash forms. Pages resolves directory indexes
# on its own; these make the canonical form explicit and keep the two spellings
# from splitting cache entries.

/orbit                    /orbit/                    301
# /starlink/ became a preset of the constellation view (plan 34 3.2 C3):
# every spelling now lands on /constellations/?c=starlink. 302, not 301 —
# public/starlink/ files still exist behind the redirect and may be deleted
# in a pure-deletion pass once the rewrite is old enough to trust.
/starlink                /constellations/?c=starlink   302
/starlink/*              /constellations/?c=starlink   302
/spacetrack               /spacetrack/               301
/spacetrack/signal        /spacetrack/signal/        301
/spacetrack/conjunctions  /spacetrack/conjunctions/  301
/spacetrack/brief         /spacetrack/brief/         301
/spacetrack/analytics     /spacetrack/analytics/     301
/admin                   /admin/                    301
/about                   /about/                    301
/wiki                    /wiki/                     301
